    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="0917" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.24B/3–746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Key</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-07T19:00:00+01:00">March 7, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 8—10:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1210. Within framework of US plans for future of Italian Air Force (see cable
                    from Military Attaché<anchor n="30" xml:id="d610-f1"/> here to War Department
                    Mar No. 84 dated 12 February 1946<anchor n="31" xml:id="d610-f2"/>) Embassy
                    supports MA’s (Military Attaché’s) view that US position in Italy would be
                    strengthened by using surplus US aviation equipment at present available in
                    European Theater to equip Italian Air Forces.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Key</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
